date-released: 2026-10-19
title: "Machina Pauliana: Modelling actio pauliana in Dutch insolvency law"
abstract: >-
  A neuro-symbolic model of the actio pauliana of Article 42 of the Dutch
  Bankruptcy Act (Faillissementswet, Fw), which allows an insolvency
  practitioner to avoid transactions that prejudice creditors. Its symbolic
  core is written in Catala in a literate style that keeps statute and
  formalisation aligned, with open-textured terms represented as boolean inputs
  where neural components couple to the symbolic solver. A neural routine
  structures a case's natural-language facts into boolean and date inputs.
  Neural subroutines resolve the open-textured terms through case-based
  reasoning over Dutch civil judgments from rechtspraak.nl, retrieved through a
  pipeline that filters on the requirement being resolved and expands along the
  procedural chain of a case. The repository also contains the pipeline that
  segments and labels those judgments, together with the evaluation scripts,
  gold standards and model outputs.
